WEBVTT

NOTE Birch & Co, carrier requirements. Friday 18 September 2026. Speakers: Arno Vale, Iris Bell, Sam Rivera.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:09.000
<v Iris Bell>Arno runs our warehouse and shipping. Before Sam talks to carriers, I want him to hear what you need.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:20.000
<v Arno Vale>Two departures a week at least. The distributor won't hold more than ten days of stock, so one a week leaves them short.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.000
<v Sam Rivera>Door to door, or to a hub?

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:33.000
<v Arno Vale>Door to door, with a tail lift. Half the distributors' sites have no loading dock.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Sam Rivera>Anything that would rule a carrier out?

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:50.000
<v Arno Vale>Claims. I'd rather pay a little more per pallet than spend a month chasing a damaged one.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.000
<v Sam Rivera>And volumes, for the first six months?

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:05.000
<v Arno Vale>Forty to sixty pallets a month to start. I can firm that up once we know the distributor's first order.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:12.000
<v Iris Bell>I'll confirm the numbers to Sam once Arno has them. Sam, who are you talking to first?

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:22.000
<v Sam Rivera>Cobalt Freight, early next week, and at least one other. I'll put your requirements on one page and send it to you both today.
